# Rimvio Dual Experience (locked)

**Canonical:** `docs/RIMVIO_DUAL_EXPERIENCE.md` · ADR-058 · ADR-064

> **One Agent, Two Experiences** — **Rimvio Agent 하나**가 User Context(Execute)와 Developer Context(Build)를 제공한다. UI **AI Build** = Rimvio Agent Developer Build Mode (**별도 Agent 아님**).  
> Agent discovers **Published Capabilities** only — not Platforms. Hub = **Infrastructure · Capability · Runtime · Adapter** + Compatibility Graph.

## Stack

```text
USER:  Utterance → Intent → Capability Discovery → Execution Binding → Runtime → Prepare → Commit
DEV:   Utterance → Rimvio Agent (Build) → Platform Graph → Sandbox → Publish → Hub Registry
```

## Do

- **One Agent** — extend ADR-045 spine; Dev Build Mode is a context switch, not a second runtime package
- Agent discovers **capabilities** (`discover-capabilities`, `capability-index`) — **not** platform home URLs or Platform Discovery
- Dev work in `components/hub/dev/` + `components/hub/deploy/` — NL-first
- Publish registers **Published Capabilities** → registry — only then Agent may invoke
- Show Compatibility: Capability ↔ Runtime ↔ Infrastructure in Dev Test UI
- User UI: work log (“호텔 검색 ✓”) — hide Capability/Platform/Manifest nouns (L1)
- Side effects: `payment.prepare` until human `payment.commit` (booking · payment)
- Extend Platform OS via `lib/platform-sdk/` — do not reinvent permission/registry/runtime

## Don't

- User Agent + Dev Agent as two products or two runtime packages
- “AI Builder Agent” as separate from Rimvio Agent
- Agent Platform Discovery (`OsakaStay` as discovery target)
- Direct vendor API from Globe chat bypassing registry
- Hub as Capability-Registry-only in docs/diagrams (omit Runtime/Infra/Adapter)
- `payment.process` in capability contracts
- Auto Commit on booking/payment from agent
- Parallel discovery stores beside capability-index + workspace

## Reference vertical

OsakaStay (`hotel.search` → `booking.prepare` → `payment.prepare` → user approval → `payment.commit` → `booking.confirm`) — published **capabilities**, not Globe-only hacks.

## PR reject

- User-facing “Capability”“Manifest” in hero/empty states
- Agent tool invoke before capability discovery on search flows
- Publish path that skips registry registration
- Docs/copy implying two Agents or Platform Discovery
